  "title": "this, call, apply, bind",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Four rules (plain functions)\n\n`obj.method()` sets `this` to `obj`. A bare `fn()` loses that receiver. `fn.call(obj)` / `apply` pick `this`. `fn.bind(obj)` returns a new function with `this` locked.\n\nAfter `const go = obj.go; go()`, the call site lost the receiver. Bind a mover so the callback still walks east.\n\nThe desk pulls `go` off the fox’s route card and later calls `go()`. Without `bind`, `this.dir` is gone and the fox stands still."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "detached",
      "promptMd": "After `const go = obj.go; go()` (plain function method), `this` is usually…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "obj",
          "md": "`obj`"
        },
        {
          "id": "lost",
          "md": "Not `obj` — the call site lost the receiver"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "lost"
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "this-lost",
      "kind": "cloze",
      "promptMd": "After `const go = obj.go; go()`, `this` is {{a}}.",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "not obj",
              "md": "not obj"
            },
            {
              "id": "obj",
              "md": "obj"
            },
            {
              "id": "the fox",
              "md": "the fox"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
